  "mode_limits": [
    "The vendor branch of --check-one only loads and merges the device manifest and parses the device compatibility matrix; it does not compare framework and vendor requirements or validate service implementations.",
    "The system branch also checks framework matrix HAL names against interface metadata compiled into this host binary. The retained stock framework result is not an assembled Evolution product check.",
    "--check-one returns before kernel argument handling. A staged kernel.config does not mean its requirements were checked.",
    "Host APEX discovery defaults apex.all.ready to true and selects active entries by their exact partition and moduleName. The complete observed list is retained, but only vendor/ODM APEX content is covered.",
    "checkvintf is not an AVB signature verifier. Its default compatibility flags exclude AVB-version comparison; the static runtime provider does not measure the running kernel SELinux policy capability."
  ],
